103
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:47,431
What do I need to remember?

104
00:06:47,967 --> 00:06:52,816
Bisect = binary search through history between a good and a bad commit.

105
00:06:53,367 --> 00:07:02,976
Automate with git bisect run SCRIPT (0 good, 1–124 bad, 125 skip).

106
00:07:03,533 --> 00:07:06,558
Always git bisect reset at the end.

107
00:07:08,300 --> 00:07:10,884
What should I know about Git blame?

108
00:07:11,433 --> 00:07:17,978
git blame FILE shows, for every line, the commit that last changed it, who made it and when.

109
00:07:17,978 --> 00:07:24,166
It answers "why is this line like this?", by leading you to the commit and its message.

110
00:07:24,166 --> 00:07:27,723
It is a research tool, not a tool to blame people.

111
00:07:29,467 --> 00:07:33,866
First, a fresh practice repository for this lesson.

112
