129
00:08:35,100 --> 00:08:37,399
Can you show me Git clean?

130
00:08:37,933 --> 00:08:40,716
git clean deletes untracked files:

131
00:08:40,716 --> 00:08:44,236
build output, temporary files, experiments.

132
00:08:44,236 --> 00:08:48,492
They are not in Git, so nothing can bring them back.

133
00:08:48,492 --> 00:08:52,093
That is why we always preview with -n first.

134
00:08:53,833 --> 00:08:58,233
First, a fresh practice repository for this lesson.

135
00:08:58,767 --> 00:09:00,957
Without -f, Git refuses:

136
00:09:00,957 --> 00:09:04,791
Preview, then clean files and directories:

137
00:09:05,333 --> 00:09:09,053
Preview, then clean files and directories:

138
00:09:09,600 --> 00:09:10,899
.env survived:

139
00:09:10,899 --> 00:09:14,519
ignored files are only removed with -x.

140
00:09:16,267 --> 00:09:17,840
Let me try something.

141
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:22,336
"Make it like a fresh clone", with -x and without a preview:

142
00:09:22,900 --> 00:09:29,012
.env held local settings and a password that are not in Git (on purpose:

143
00:09:29,012 --> 00:09:29,946
lesson 73).

144
00:09:29,946 --> 00:09:35,039
git clean does not use a trash bin, the reflog or the stash:

145
