150
00:09:52,247 --> 00:09:54,998
What do I need to remember?

151
00:09:55,533 --> 00:10:00,448
git clean permanently deletes untracked files; it requires -f.

152
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:07,369
Always run -n first; -d for directories; -x/-X for ignored files.

153
00:10:07,933 --> 00:10:13,788
Keep templates (.env.example) for anything local you might wipe.

154
00:10:15,533 --> 00:10:18,611
I keep hearing about .gitignore.

155
00:10:18,611 --> 00:10:20,438
What is it, really?

156
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:24,335
.gitignore lists files Git should not track:

157
00:10:24,335 --> 00:10:29,337
dependencies, build output, logs, local configuration and secrets.

158
00:10:29,337 --> 00:10:35,401
We write patterns, test them with git check-ignore, and fix the classic problem:

159
00:10:35,401 --> 00:10:40,024
a file that is already tracked is not affected by .gitignore.

160
00:10:41,767 --> 00:10:46,166
First, a fresh practice repository for this lesson.

161
00:10:46,700 --> 00:10:50,977
Only .gitignore and keep.log are left as untracked.

162
00:10:50,977 --> 00:10:52,989
Which rule matches what?

163
00:10:53,533 --> 00:10:57,810
Only .gitignore and keep.log are left as untracked.

164
00:10:57,810 --> 00:10:59,823
Which rule matches what?

165
00:11:00,367 --> 00:11:01,966
Let's run it.

166
00:11:03,700 --> 00:11:05,392
Let me try something.

167
00:11:05,392 --> 00:11:11,194
A config file was committed long ago; now someone adds it to .gitignore:

168
00:11:11,733 --> 00:11:12,932
M config.local:

169
00:11:12,932 --> 00:11:15,888
still tracked, still showing changes.

170
00:11:15,888 --> 00:11:23,878
.gitignore only affects untracked files; Git keeps tracking every file that is already in the index.

171
00:11:25,633 --> 00:11:31,958
Remove it from the index (not from disk), commit, and it becomes an ignored file:

172
00:11:33,700 --> 00:11:34,413
Got it.

173
00:11:34,413 --> 00:11:37,164
What do I need to remember?

174
00:11:37,700 --> 00:11:44,169
.gitignore patterns keep dependencies, build output, logs and secrets out of Git.

175
00:11:44,733 --> 00:11:48,198
git check-ignore -v explains which rule applies.

176
00:11:48,733 --> 00:11:50,921
Tracked files are not affected:

177
00:11:50,921 --> 00:11:55,578
git rm --cached, commit, and rotate any secret that was committed.
